1
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,920
Before the first login,

2
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:14,540
before the screens glow,

3
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:18,400
someone keeps the signal moving.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:22,820
through the systems down below.

5
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:46,080
Under every cloud,

6
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,980
behind every stream,

7
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:50,200
there is a night shift.

8
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,580
inside the machine.

9
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,860
WiFi in the hallway,

10
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:55,520
uplinks in the rack,

11
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:57,520
failover waiting.

12
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:59,360
when the main path cracks.

13
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:02,320
When the lights turn red,

14
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:05,940
when the alarms begin,

15
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,240
they read the storm,

16
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:12,860
then bring the green back in.

17
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:17,140
Network engineers,

18
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:19,340
hold the line.

19
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:21,000
Network engineers,

20
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,900
keep the world online.

21
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,880
From edge to core,

22
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:26,400
from port to route,

23
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:28,600
they keep the packets moving.

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,860
when the noise breaks out.

25
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,600
Link up.

26
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:38,440
Route clean.

27
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:40,160
Ports live.

28
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,060
Packets move.

29
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:46,000
No one sees.

30
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,160
Still they move.

31
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,700
You touch the app,

32
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:15,580
they guard the path.

33
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:17,580
You call it simple,

34
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,420
they know the math.

35
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:21,540
Between the outage.

36
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:22,920
and the final screen,

37
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:25,120
they find the fault.

38
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,800
inside the unseen.

39
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,500
Network engineers,

40
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,700
hold the line.

41
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:33,420
Network engineers,

42
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,420
keep the world online.

43
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:37,340
Layer by layer,

44
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:39,300
night after night,

45
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,100
they keep the service breathing.

46
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:43,180
until the graphs turn bright.
